      "message": "Note: Initially I wanted to have a separate resources/sksl/glsl/Sampler2DRect.sksl for the supported GLSL case and a resources/sksl/errors/Sampler2DRect.sksl for the unsupported Metal/SPIR-V case. I had to abandon that approach because files under errors/ are fed to SkSLErrorTest which currently doesn\u0027t support different error/GLSL messages per-backend and I didn\u0027t want to add a special rule to skip only this test.\n\nI\u0027m considering adding support to SkSLErrorTest so that a shader can specify per-backend error messages. If folks are supportive, I can follow up with that change so we have some automation around the error messages I added here.",
